R:Adam R is a researcher who co-authored the study protocol of the PROPILS trial.SA CUNHA A:Sa Cunha A is a researcher involved in the PROPILS trial.CHERQUI D:Cherqui D is a researcher who contributed to the PROPILS trial study protocol.SCHIELKE A:Schielke A is a researcher involved in the study of preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer.SOUBRANE O:Soubrane O is a researcher who co-authored the study protocol of the PROPILS trial.SCATTON O:Scatton O is a researcher involved in the PROPILS trial.SALLOUM C:Salloum C is a researcher who contributed to the PROPILS trial study protocol.AZOULAY D:Azoulay D is a researcher involved in the study of preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer.BENOIST S:Benoist S is a researcher who co-authored the study protocol of the PROPILS trial.GOYER P:Goyer P is a researcher involved in the PROPILS trial.VAILLANT JC:Vaillant JC is a researcher who contributed to the PROPILS trial study protocol.HANNOUN L:Hannoun L is a researcher involved in the study of preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer.BOLESLAWSKI E:Boleslawski E is a researcher who co-authored the study protocol of the PROPILS trial.AGOSTINI H:Agostini H is a researcher involved in the PROPILS trial.SAMUEL D:Samuel D is a researcher who contributed to the PROPILS trial study protocol.CASTAING D:Castaing D is a researcher involved in the study of preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer.CIACIO O:FISIOPATOLOG√çA DE LA HIPONATREMIA:The pathophysiology of hyponatremia, discussed in the context of patients receiving artificial nutritionMANIFESTACIONES CL√çNICAS DE LA HIPONATREMIA:Clinical manifestations of hyponatremia, which are important for diagnosis in patients with artificial nutritionDIAGN√ìSTICO Y ETIOLOG√çA DE LA HIPONATREMIA:Diagnosis and etiology of hyponatremia in patients receiving artificial nutritionTRATAMIENTO DE LA HIPONATREMIA:Treatment of hyponatremia in the context of artificial nutritionSRAA:The SRAA, or Sistema Renina-Angiotensina-Aldosterona, is a crucial hormonal system that plays a significant role in regulating blood pressure and maintaining fluid balance within the body. This system operates by coordinating the actions of various hormones, including renin, angiotensin, and aldosterone. It is important to note that the SRAA is inhibited during antidiuresis, a process mediated by antidiuretic hormone (ADH), which further influences fluid retention and blood pressure regulation. Overall, the SRAA is essential for homeostasis, ensuring that blood pressure remains stable and that the body's fluid levels are appropriately managed.N. PARAVENTRICULAR:The paraventricular nucleus is a part of the hypothalamus that plays a role in the secretion of hormones including ADH.N. SUPRA√ìPTICO:The supraoptic nucleus is another part of the hypothalamus involved in the production of ADH.H2O:Water (H2O) is the primary substance regulated by ADH in the body.ACUAPORINAS:Aquaporins are water channel proteins that facilitate the transport of water across cell membranes, regulated by ADH.HORMONA ADRENOCORTICOTROPA:BLOQUE: SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO:A section or block focused on advanced nutritional support, particularly in relation to maintaining body water in threatening situationsNEUROLOGICAL MANIFESTATIONS:Clinical symptoms related to the nervous system that arise from hyponatremia, including headache, lethargy, confusion, and severe outcomes like coma and seizuresNEUROHYPOPHYSIS:The part of the pituitary gland that releases ADH, playing a crucial role in water retention and the development of conditions like SIADHP√âPTIDO NATRIUR√âTICO ATRIAL:A hormone that promotes sodium excretion and is involved in the body's response to increased plasma volumeGLUTAMATO:Glutamato is an organic molecule that serves as a neurotransmitter in the brain, playing a role in the body's response to cerebral edema during hyponatremia.INOSITOL:Inositol is an organic compound that is involved in the cellular processes and may help in reducing cerebral edema during hyponatremia.PROTE√çNAS TOTALES:Prote√≠nas totales refer to the total amount of proteins in the blood, which can influence sodium measurements and the diagnosis of hyponatremia.ESPANOL:El territorio espa√±ol es el √°rea geogr√°fica donde se realizan estudios sobre la natremia y la hiponatremia en pacientes.HIPOPROTEINEMIA:La hipoproteinemia es una condici√≥n m√©dica caracterizada por niveles bajos de prote√≠nas en la sangre, que puede influir en la natremia.EDEMA PULMONAR:El edema pulmonar es una condici√≥n m√©dica que puede ser un signo de hiponatremia hipervol√©mica y se caracteriza por la acumulaci√≥n de l√≠quido en los pulmones.ORTOSTATISMO:El ortostatismo es una condici√≥n que se refiere a la ca√≠da de la presi√≥n arterial al ponerse de pie, que puede indicar hipovolemia en pacientes con hiponatremia.CIRROSIS HEPATICA:Cirrhosis hep√°tica is a late stage of scarring (fibrosis) of the liver caused by many forms of liver diseases and conditions, such as hepatitis and chronic alcoholism.DIUR√âTICOS TIAZIDA:Diur√©ticos tiazida are a class of diuretics that are commonly used to treat high blood pressure and can cause hiponatremia in some patients.DIUR√âTICOS DEL GRUPO TIAZIDA:Diur√©ticos del grupo tiazida are a class of medications commonly used to treat high blood pressure and fluid retention, which can lead to conditions like hiponatremia in some patients.INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL PRIMARIA:Insuficiencia suprarrenal primaria is a condition where the adrenal glands do not produce sufficient steroid hormones, which can contribute to electrolyte imbalances such as hyperkalemia and metabolic acidosis.GTTK:GTTK is a diagnostic test used to evaluate the function of mineralocorticoid receptors and assess aldosterone levels in patients with suspected adrenal insufficiency.ELLISON DH:Ellison DH is a researcher who contributed to the understanding of SIADH and its diagnostic criteria, as referenced in the New England Journal of Medicine.VERBALIS ET AL.:Verbalis et al. are researchers who provided insights into the main causes of SIADH, as referenced in The American Journal of Medicine.SISTEMA NERVIOSO CENTRAL:The "SISTEMA NERVIOSO CENTRAL" (central nervous system, CNS) plays a vital role in the proper development of swallowing and feeding behaviors in children. Additionally, the CNS can be impacted by a range of disorders, such as tumors and inflammatory diseases, which may result in conditions like Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion (SIADH). This highlights the importance of the CNS not only in developmental processes but also in its susceptibility to various medical conditions.FARMACOL√ìGICO:Pharmacological factors can stimulate the secretion of ADH, leading to SIADH, as discussed in the text.HIPOANTREMIA:HIPOANTREMIA refers to a common water metabolism disorder known as hiponatremia, which is particularly prevalent among hospitalized patients, especially those who are receiving artificial nutrition.SOLUCI√ìN SALINA HIPERT√ìNICA:Soluci√≥n Salina Hipert√≥nica is a medical treatment used to correct severe hyponatremia by providing a high concentration of sodium to help reduce cerebral edema.S√çNDROME DE DESMIELINIZACI√ìN OSM√ìTICA:S√≠ndrome de Desmielinizaci√≥n Osm√≥tica is a serious neurological condition that can occur as a complication of rapid correction of chronic hyponatremia.TRATAMIENTO ADECUADO:Adequate treatment refers to the specific medical interventions tailored to correct hyponatremia based on its type and etiology.REVIEWS IN CLINICAL GERONTOLOGY:Reviews in Clinical Gerontology is a publication that features studies and reviews related to clinical gerontology, including topics like hyponatremia.SUERO GLUCOSADO:SUERO GLUCOSADO, or glucose solution, is a type of intravenous fluid utilized in medical treatments. It plays a crucial role in managing sodium levels in patients and is particularly important in the treatment of hyponatremia. This solution is often used in conjunction with treatments for patients receiving artificial nutrition, aiding in the management of fluid balance.D√âFICIT DE ATENCI√ìN:Deficit de atenci√≥n refers to attention deficits, which can occur in patients with hyponatremia and is categorized under mild neurological symptoms.ALT. MEMORIA:Alteraciones de memoria refers to memory disturbances, which can be symptoms of hyponatremia and are categorized under mild neurological symptoms.MARCHA INESTABLE:Marcha inestable refers to unstable gait, which can be a symptom of hyponatremia and is categorized under mild neurological symptoms.ALT. COGNITIVA:Alteraciones cognitivas refer to cognitive disturbances, which can occur in patients with hyponatremia and are categorized under mild neurological symptoms.DESORIENTACI√ìN:Desorientaci√≥n refers to disorientation, which can be a symptom of hyponatremia and is categorized under moderate neurological symptoms.SOMNOLENCIA:Somnolencia refers to drowsiness, which can be a symptom of hyponatremia and is categorized under moderate neurological symptoms.CONFUSI√ìN:Confusi√≥n refers to confusion, which can be a symptom of hyponatremia and is categorized under moderate neurological symptoms.ESTUPOR:Estupor refers to stupor, which can be a severe symptom of hyponatremia.DISTRES RESPIRATORIO:Distress respiratorio refers to respiratory distress, which can be a severe symptom of hyponatremia.HIPONATREMIA HIPOVOL√âMICA:Hiponatremia hipovol√©mica refers to a type of hyponatremia caused by low blood volume.HIPONATREMIA EUVOL√âMICA:Hiponatremia euvol√©mica es una condici√≥n m√©dica que se presenta en pacientes que reciben nutrici√≥n artificial. Se caracteriza por niveles bajos de sodio en la sangre, pero sin una disminuci√≥n del volumen de l√≠quido corporal. En este tipo de hiponatremia, el volumen sangu√≠neo se mantiene normal, lo que distingue a esta condici√≥n de otras formas de hiponatremia que pueden estar asociadas con una reducci√≥n del volumen de l√≠quido.HIPONATREMIA HIPERVOL√âMICA:Hiponatremia hipervol√©mica refers to a type of hyponatremia caused by high blood volume.CIRROSIS CON ASCITIS:Cirrhosis con ascitis refers to cirrhosis with ascites, which can lead to hypervolemic hyponatremia.CONIVAPT√ÅN:Conivapt√°n is a medication that functions as a vasopressin receptor antagonist, specifically designed to treat hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood. It is administered intravenously and works by antagonizing the effects of antidiuretic hormone (ADH), thereby helping to restore normal sodium levels in patients.FURST:La f√≥rmula de Furst es un c√°lculo utilizado para estimar la capacidad renal de eliminar agua libre, relevante en el manejo de la hiponatremia.INTOXICACI√ìN AGUDA DE AGUA:La intoxicaci√≥n aguda de agua es una condici√≥n que puede llevar a hiponatremia, resultando de la ingesta excesiva de agua en un corto per√≠odo de tiempo.FURSEMIDE:Furosemide is a medication used to promote the elimination of free water in patients with SIADH, administered either intravenously or orally.AZOTEMIA:Azotemia is a medical condition characterized by an excess of nitrogenous waste products in the blood, often due to kidney dysfunction.FURST FORMULA:The Furst formula is a calculation utilized in the medical field to estimate renal capacity for eliminating free water, particularly in patients diagnosed with Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). Additionally, it serves as a method for calculating sodium and potassium levels in patients experiencing hyponatremia. This dual application highlights the formula's importance in managing electrolyte imbalances and assessing renal function in specific clinical scenarios.ALGORITMO MULTIDISCIPLINAR:The "ALGORITMO MULTIDISCIPLINAR" is a comprehensive multidisciplinary algorithm designed for the management of hyponatremia, particularly in cases secondary to the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). This algorithm offers detailed guidelines for treatment options, ensuring effective management of hyponatremia in patients. It is especially relevant for individuals receiving artificial nutrition, providing tailored recommendations to address their specific needs. Overall, the algorithm serves as a crucial tool for healthcare professionals in optimizing the care of patients with hyponatremia.HEMORRAGIA SUBARACNOIDEA:Hemorragia subaracnoidea (Subarachnoid Hemorrhage) is a condition that can lead to SIADH and has a specific treatment duration.MASAS CEREBRALES:Masas cerebrales (Brain Tumors) can cause SIADH and affect treatment duration based on the underlying disease evolution.LESIONES CEREBRALES INFLAMATORIAS:Lesiones cerebrales inflamatorias (Inflammatory Brain Injuries) can induce SIADH and affect treatment response.IDIOP√ÅTICO:Idiop√°tico (Idiopathic) refers to cases of SIADH with no known cause, affecting treatment duration.ELEVADAS TRANSAMINASAS:Elevated transaminases refer to a potential side effect of medications, which is monitored during treatment for SIADH.AGUAS:FURSEMIDA:FURSEMIDA, also known as Furosemide, is a diuretic medication primarily utilized to treat fluid retention. It is particularly effective in managing conditions associated with excess fluid accumulation in the body. Additionally, Furosemide is employed in the treatment of patients experiencing hyponatremia, especially those who are receiving artificial nutrition. This medication plays a crucial role in regulating fluid balance and electrolyte levels in various clinical settings.HIPOANTREMIA GRAVE:Severe hyponatremia is a critical condition that requires immediate medical intervention, often involving hypertonic saline.HIPO-NATREMIA:Hipo-natremia refers to a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, which can be caused by various factors including fluid imbalance and hormonal issues.HIPO-NATREMIA HIPOVOL√âMICA:Hypo-natremia hypovolemic is a specific type of hyponatremia caused by a decrease in blood volume, often due to fluid loss.HIPO-NATREMIA HIPERVOLEMICA:Hypo-natremia hypervolemic is a type of hyponatremia that occurs when there is an excess of fluid in the body, diluting sodium levels.SFS:SFS (Saline Solution) is a solution used for rehydration and electrolyte balanceNUTRICI√ìN AVANZADA:Advanced Nutrition refers to specialized nutritional support strategies used in complex medical conditionsINSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA AGUDA:Acute heart failure is a sudden inability of the heart to pump effectively, which can lead to fluid overload and hyponatremiaHYPOANTREMIA:Hyponatremia is a medical condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, which can lead to various health complications.SALT-1 TRIAL:The SALT-1 trial is a clinical study that evaluated the efficacy of tolvaptan in patients with the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion.SALT-2 TRIAL:The SALT-2 trial is a clinical study that further assessed the use of tolvaptan in treating hyponatremia.CLINICAL ENDOCRINOLOGY:Clinical Endocrinology is a journal dedicated to publishing research and reviews on various aspects of clinical endocrinology. It focuses on a range of topics, including adrenal insufficiency and hyponatremia, providing a platform for studies that contribute to the understanding and management of these conditions. The journal serves as a valuable resource for professionals in the field, facilitating the dissemination of important findings and advancements in endocrinology.NEPHRON PHYSIOLOGY:Nephron Physiology is a journal that focuses on research related to kidney function and disorders, including hyponatremia.INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF KIDNEY DISEASES:The International Journal of Kidney Diseases publishes research related to kidney health, including studies on hyponatremia and its effects.MOUNT DB:Mount DB is an author of a study on mortality after hospitalization with hyponatremia.CURHAN GC:Curhan GC is an author of a study on mortality after hospitalization with hyponatremia.HOORN EJ:Hoorn EJ is a researcher and author who has focused on the effects of mild hyponatremia on health outcomes. Through their studies, Hoorn EJ has contributed to the understanding of hyponatremia and its clinical implications, highlighting its significance in medical research and patient care.ZIETSE R:Zietse R is an author who has contributed to research on hyponatremia and its effects on mortality.ANDERSON RJ:Anderson RJ is an author who has conducted a prospective analysis of hyponatremia's epidemiology.CHUNG HM:Chung HM is an author involved in research on hyponatremia and its clinical outcomes.KLUGE R:Kluge R is an author who has studied the epidemiology of hyponatremia.SCHRIER RW:Schrier RW is a co-author who has contributed to research on oral tolvaptan, a medication used in the treatment of certain conditions related to fluid balance. Additionally, Schrier RW has conducted research on the pathogenetic role of vasopressin in hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood. Through these contributions, Schrier RW has played a significant role in advancing the understanding of vasopressin's impact on fluid regulation and its implications for hyponatremia.GILL GV:Gill GV is an author who has studied the characteristics and outcomes of severe hyponatremia.HUDA MSB:Huda MSB is an author who has contributed to research on severe hyponatremia.WILE D:Wile D is an author involved in the study of severe hyponatremia.BOYD A:Boyd A is an author who has researched the outcomes of severe hyponatremia.SKAGEN K:Skagen K is an author who has studied the characteristics of severe hyponatremia.WATSON ID:Watson ID is an author who has contributed to research on severe hyponatremia.CHAWLA A:Chawla A is an author who has studied the mortality associated with hyponatremia.STEARNS RH:Stearns RH is an author who has researched hyponatremia as a risk factor for inpatient mortality.NIGWEKAR SU:Nigwekar SU is an author