ganization that studies the relationship between diet and cancer risk, particularly focusing on red and processed meat consumption.NI√ëO:A child who is the subject of dietary recommendations and nutritional needs.DEPORTE:Sports activities are mentioned in relation to children's increased nutritional requirements and dietary adjustments.DOM√çNGUEZ ORTEGA:F. Dom√≠nguez Ortega is an author who analyzed the concentration of fatty acids in colostrum and transitional milk.MART√çNEZ SU√ÅREZ:Mart√≠nez Su√°rez is an author who provided recommendations on calcium and vitamin D intake for children.WAGNER CL.:Wagner CL. is an author associated with the American Academy of Pediatrics, focusing on the prevention of rickets and vitamin D deficiency.KOLETZKO B.:Koletzko B. is an author who contributed to the global standard for the composition of infant formula.REAL DECRETO 867/2008:REAL DECRETO 867/2008 is a Spanish regulation that establishes technical and sanitary standards for the production of infant formulas and follow-up formulas. It governs the composition and safety of these products, ensuring that they meet specific technical-sanitary regulations in Spain. This regulation plays a crucial role in safeguarding the health and well-being of infants by setting clear guidelines for the formulation and quality of infant nutrition products.GUIDELINE ON FLUORIDE THERAPY:The Guideline on Fluoride Therapy provides recommendations for the use of fluoride in pediatric dentistry.TORUN B.:ANA BEL√âN MART√çNEZ ZAZO:Ana Bel√©n Mart√≠nez Zazo is a pediatric specialist and attending physician at Hospital La Moraleja in Madrid, focusing on pediatric nutrition.√ìSCAR RUBIO CABEZAS:√ìscar Rubio Cabezas is a pediatric specialist and researcher at Hospital Infantil Universitario Ni√±o Jes√∫s in Madrid, with a focus on pediatric endocrinology.CONSUELO PEDR√ìN GINER:Consuelo Pedr√≥n Giner is a pediatric specialist and doctor at Hospital Infantil Universitario Ni√±o Jes√∫s in Madrid, specializing in nutrition and gastroenterology.HOSPITAL LA MORALEJA:Hospital La Moraleja is a medical facility in Madrid specializing in pediatric care.HOSPITAL INFANTIL UNIVERSITARIO NI√ëO JES√öS:Hospital Infantil Universitario Ni√±o Jes√∫s is a children's hospital in Madrid that provides specialized pediatric care and research.LANCET ONCOLOGY:Lancet Oncology is a medical journal that publishes research on cancer, including studies on dietary impacts on cancer risk.ALIMENTOS NATURALES:ALIMENTOS NATURALES refers to natural food sources that are utilized in the preparation of nutritional formulas specifically designed for enteral feeding. These foods are also suitable for supplementing the oral diet of pediatric patients, providing essential nutrients in a natural form to support their dietary needs.M√ìDULOS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional modules that can be used to enhance the diet of children with inadequate oral intake.PACIENTES PEDI√ÅTRICOS:S√çNDROME DE INMUNODEFICIENCIA ADQUIRIDA:A condition that can lead to increased nutritional needs and may require enteral feeding.ATRESIA ESOF√ÅGICA:Esophageal atresia is a congenital condition where the esophagus does not connect properly, necessitating enteral nutrition.F√çSTULA TRAQUEOESOF√ÅGICA:Tracheoesophageal fistula is a congenital defect that can complicate feeding, often requiring enteral nutrition.S√çNDROME DE PIERRE-ROBIN:Pierre-Robin syndrome is a condition that can cause feeding difficulties, often requiring enteral nutrition.NEFROPAT√çA CR√ìNICA:Chronic kidney disease can affect nutritional status, often necessitating enteral nutrition.FUNDUPLICATURA DE NISSEN:FUNDUPLICATURA DE NISSEN is a surgical technique used to prevent gastroesophageal reflux, often associated with gastrostomy procedures.PSEUDOBSTRUCCI√ìN INTESTINAL CR√ìNICA:PSEUDOBSTRUCCI√ìN INTESTINAL CR√ìNICA is a medical condition characterized by symptoms of intestinal blockage without any physical obstruction.ALTERACIONES EN LA EXCRECI√ìN DE NUTRIENTES:ALTERACIONES EN LA EXCRECI√ìN DE NUTRIENTES refers to changes in the body's ability to absorb and excrete nutrients, often impacting overall health.FUNDUPLICATURA:La funduplicatura es un procedimiento quir√∫rgico indicado en casos de enfermedad pulmonar asociada al reflujo gastroesof√°gico.BOT√ìN DE GASTROSTOM√çA:El bot√≥n de gastrostom√≠a es un dispositivo que permite la colocaci√≥n de una v√°lvula unidireccional en el punto de inserci√≥n de la gastrostom√≠a.YEYUNOSTOM√çAS QUIR√öRGICAS:Las yeyunostom√≠as quir√∫rgicas son procedimientos indicados en pacientes con reflujo gastroesof√°gico grave o gastroparesia no controlable.SONDAS TRANSIL√ìRICAS:Las sondas transpil√≥ricas son dispositivos que se pueden colocar a trav√©s de gastrostom√≠as preexistentes para la alimentaci√≥n enteral.BOMBAS DE NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL:Las bombas de nutrici√≥n enteral son dispositivos utilizados para administrar f√≥rmulas enterales de manera controlada y precisa.ALIMENTACI√ìN G√ÅSTRICA INTERMITENTE:La alimentaci√≥n g√°strica intermitente es una t√©cnica de administraci√≥n de f√≥rmulas enterales en forma de bolo, facilitando la transici√≥n a la ingesta oral.NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL A D√âBITO CONTINUO:La nutrici√≥n enteral a d√©bito continuo se administra con una bomba de infusi√≥n perist√°ltica, indicada en pacientes con disminuci√≥n del √°rea absortiva intestinal.GASTROPEXIA:La gastropexia es una t√©cnica quir√∫rgica utilizada para fijar el est√≥mago a la pared abdominal, facilitando la colocaci√≥n de una sonda de gastrostom√≠a.F√ìRMULAS COMERCIALES:Commercially prepared nutritional formulas made from various natural food sources, designed for enteral feeding.F√ìRMULAS A PARTIR DE ALIMENTOS NATURALES:Nutritional formulas made from natural food sources like meat, eggs, and vegetables, suitable for patients with adequate digestive capacity.NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL C√çCLICA:A method of enteral nutrition that combines formula administration during specific hours and intermittent oral feeding.PEDIATRIC FORMULAS:Pediatric formulas are specially designed nutritional products for children aged 1 to 10 years, providing essential vitamins and minerals.DIETIST:A dietist is a professional who specializes in diet and nutrition, playing a crucial role in the assessment and management of malnutrition. They assist in calculating nutritional compositions to ensure that patients achieve adequate nutrient intake, thereby promoting overall health and well-being.CHRONIC NEUROLOGICAL DISEASES:Chronic neurological diseases are conditions that require long-term nutritional support due to compromised digestive functions.MODULAR COMPONENTS:Modular components are nutritional supplements used to modify enteral formulas to meet specific dietary needs.FORMULAS FOR CHILDREN:Formulas for children are specialized nutritional products designed to meet the dietary needs of children over 10 years old.ENSURE JUNIOR DRINK:Ensure Junior Drink is a nutritional formula produced by Abbott, designed for children aged 1-10 years, providing essential nutrients and energy for growth.ENSURE JUNIOR PLUS:Ensure Junior Plus is a nutritional formula produced by Abbott, aimed at children aged 1-10 years, offering additional protein and energy.ENSURE JUNIOR CON FIBRA:Ensure Junior con fibra is a nutritional formula by Abbott, tailored for children aged 1-10 years, enriched with fiber for digestive health.ENSURE JUNIOR PLUS CON FIBRA:Ensure Junior Plus con Fibra is a nutritional formula from Abbott, designed for children aged 1-10 years, combining extra protein and fiber.FREBINI ORIGINAL:Frebini original is a nutritional formula produced by Fresenius-Kabi, suitable for children aged 1-12 years, providing essential nutrients.FORTINI 1.0 MULTI FIBRE:Fortini 1.0 Multi Fibre is a nutritional formula by Nutricia, designed for children aged 1-12 years, offering a balanced mix of nutrients and fiber.FORTINI:Fortini is a nutritional formula produced by Nutricia, suitable for children from 1 year old, providing essential nutrients for growth.F