ΩÂô¬;Õ¿º$ò<f^,=Eë¸º2c=é·A<¸<G•k∫ˆ'ºKDvºú—¨ºvb:}S;ës<Ôéº¬|{<Ç¢<EﬁßªÍ¬Dª÷ßèºÖ›åªü™=±:±∫û †ºåU;cÖ¡<:?xº␀ =d‘¥<ù”tªª»›;Ì◊◊<Æ`"Ω‰”¢º¬=:,Ω8*ÂºeöT∫ πlº†5≥ªÏ’ªﬁ‰Äº0£<DÌ<›ñ±º0∞ß<Mº Øº–ÙïºÅÚ˙º	|Ö<ó {:ZÇ0= òªò3∆;^˛:πw¢ªDí<2␀øªˇfÕ<óm¶∫f"Ñ<I}2ºæe ΩÎLº<%öÀº:∆É;√é"ΩçWJπãDˇ;¥ãl<Qü;kƒ˙º˘;<9=0Ωpu¨ºé·AªV‚Å<‚S<¶ö]<@∏;ŒX˜ºçWJ<5v<j¡º=‹:ºÑSïº(Æ∫∫5“<-`<{"title": "WORLD J SURG:World J Surg is a journal that published a summary of research on perioperative immunonutrition in surgical cancer patients."}{"title": "EUR J SURG:Eur J Surg is a journal that published studies on the immune and nutritional effects of early enteral nutrition after major abdominal operations."}{"title": "VORON T:Voron T is a researcher who co-authored the study protocol of the PROPILS trial."}{"title": "PITTAU G:Pittau G is a researcher involved in the PROPILS trial studying preoperative immunonutrition."}{"title": "LEWIN M:Lewin M is a researcher who contributed to the PROPILS trial study protocol."}{"title": "VIBERT E:Vibert E is a researcher involved in the study of preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer."}{"title": "ADAM R:Adam R is a researcher who co-authored the study protocol of the PROPILS trial."}{"title": "SA CUNHA A:Sa Cunha A is a researcher involved in the PROPILS trial."}{"title": "CHERQUI D:Cherqui D is a researcher who contributed to the PROPILS trial study protocol."}{"title": "SCHIELKE A:Schielke A is a researcher involved in the study of preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer."}{"title": "SOUBRANE O:Soubrane O is a researcher who co-authored the study protocol of the PROPILS trial."}{"title": "SCATTON O:Scatton O is a researcher involved in the PROPILS trial."}{"title": "SALLOUM C:Salloum C is a researcher who contributed to the PROPILS trial study protocol."}{"title": "AZOULAY D:Azoulay D is a researcher involved in the study of preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer."}{"title": "BENOIST S:Benoist S is a researcher who co-authored the study protocol of the PROPILS trial."}{"title": "GOYER P:Goyer P is a researcher involved in the PROPILS trial."}{"title": "VAILLANT JC:Vaillant JC is a researcher who contributed to the PROPILS trial study protocol."}{"title": "HANNOUN L:Hannoun L is a researcher involved in the study of preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer."}{"title": "BOLESLAWSKI E:Boleslawski E is a researcher who co-authored the study protocol of the PROPILS trial."}{"title": "AGOSTINI H:Agostini H is a researcher involved in the PROPILS trial."}{"title": "SAMUEL D:Samuel D is a researcher who contributed to the PROPILS trial study protocol."}{"title": "CASTAING D:Castaing D is a researcher involved in the study of preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer."}{"title": "CIACIO O:"}{"title": "FISIOPATOLOG\u00cdA DE LA HIPONATREMIA:The pathophysiology of hyponatremia, discussed in the context of patients receiving artificial nutrition"}{"title": "MANIFESTACIONES CL\u00cdNICAS DE LA HIPONATREMIA:Clinical manifestations of hyponatremia, which are important for diagnosis in patients with artificial nutrition"}{"title": "DIAGN\u00d3STICO Y ETIOLOG\u00cdA DE LA HIPONATREMIA:Diagnosis and etiology of hyponatremia in patients receiving artificial nutrition"}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO DE LA HIPONATREMIA:Treatment of hyponatremia in the context of artificial nutrition"}{"title": "SRAA:The SRAA, or Sistema Renina-Angiotensina-Aldosterona, is a crucial hormonal system that plays a significant role in regulating blood pressure and maintaining fluid balance within the body. This system operates by coordinating the actions of various hormones, including renin, angiotensin, and aldosterone. It is important to note that the SRAA is inhibited during antidiuresis, a process mediated by antidiuretic hormone (ADH), which further influences fluid retention and blood pressure regulation. Overall, the SRAA is essential for homeostasis, ensuring that blood pressure remains stable and that the body's fluid levels are appropriately managed."}{"title": "N. PARAVENTRICULAR:The paraventricular nucleus is a part of the hypothalamus that plays a role in the secretion of hormones including ADH."}{"title": "N. SUPRA\u00d3PTICO:The supraoptic nucleus is another part of the hypothalamus involved in the production of ADH."}{"title": "H2O:Water (H2O) is the primary substance regulated by ADH in the body."}{"title": "ACUAPORINAS:Aquaporins are water channel proteins that facilitate the transport of water across cell membranes, regulated by ADH."}{"title": "HORMONA ADRENOCORTICOTROPA:"}{"title": "BLOQUE: SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO:A section or block focused on advanced nutritional support, particularly in relation to maintaining body water in threatening situations"}{"title": "NEUROLOGICAL MANIFESTATIONS:Clinical symptoms related to the nervous system that arise from hyponatremia, including headache, lethargy, confusion, and severe outcomes like coma and seizures"}{"title": "NEUROHYPOPHYSIS:The part of the pituitary gland that releases ADH, playing a crucial role in water retention and the development of conditions like SIADH"}{"title": "P\u00c9PTIDO NATRIUR\u00c9TICO ATRIAL:A hormone that promotes sodium excretion and is involved in the body's response to increased plasma volume"}{"title": "GLUTAMATO:Glutamato is an organic molecule that serves as a neurotransmitter in the brain, playing a role in the body's response to cerebral edema during hyponatremia."}{"title": "INOSITOL:Inositol is an organic compound that is involved in the cellular processes and may help in reducing cerebral edema during hyponatremia."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNAS TOTALES:Prote\u00ednas totales refer to the total amount of proteins in the blood, which can influence sodium measurements and the diagnosis of hyponatremia."}{"title": "ESPANOL:El territorio espa\u00f1ol es el \u00e1rea geogr\u00e1fica donde se realizan estudios sobre la natremia y la hiponatremia en pacientes."}{"title": "HIPOPROTEINEMIA:La hipoproteinemia es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica caracterizada por niveles bajos de prote\u00ednas en la sangre, que puede influir en la natremia."}{"title": "EDEMA PULMONAR:El edema pulmonar es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que puede ser un signo de hiponatremia hipervol\u00e9mica y se caracteriza por la acumulaci\u00f3n de l\u00edquido en los pulmones."}{"title": "ORTOSTATISMO:El ortostatismo es una condici\u00f3n que se refiere a la ca\u00edda de la presi\u00f3n arterial al ponerse de pie, que puede indicar hipovolemia en pacientes con hiponatremia."}{"title": "CIRROSIS HEPATICA:Cirrhosis hep\u00e1tica is a late stage of scarring (fibrosis) of the liver caused by many forms of liver diseases and conditions, such as hepatitis and chronic alcoholism."}{"title": "DIUR\u00c9TICOS TIAZIDA:Diur\u00e9ticos tiazida are a class of diuretics that are commonly used to treat high blood pressure and can cause hiponatremia in some patients."}{"title": "DIUR\u00c9TICOS DEL GRUPO TIAZIDA:Diur\u00e9ticos del grupo tiazida are a class of medications commonly used to treat high blood pressure and fluid retention, which can lead to conditions like hiponatremia in some patients."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL PRIMARIA:Insuficiencia suprarrenal primaria is a condition where the adrenal glands do not produce sufficient steroid hormones, which can contribute to electrolyte imbalances such as hyperkalemia and metabolic acidosis."}{"title": "GTTK:GTTK is a diagnostic test used to evaluate the function of mineralocorticoid receptors and assess aldosterone levels in patients with suspected adrenal insufficiency."}{"title": "ELLISON DH:Ellison DH is a researcher who contributed to the understanding of SIADH and its diagnostic criteria, as referenced in the New England Journal of Medicine."}{"title": "VERBALIS ET AL.:Verbalis et al. are researchers who provided insights into the main causes of SIADH, as referenced in The American Journal of Medicine."}{"title": "SISTEMA NERVIOSO CENTRAL:The \"SISTEMA NERVIOSO CENTRAL\" (central nervous system, CNS) plays a vital role in the proper development of swallowing and feeding behaviors in children. Additionally, the CNS can be impacted by a range of disorders, such as tumors and inflammatory diseases, which may result in conditions like Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion (SIADH). This highlights the importance of the CNS not only in developmental processes but also in its susceptibility to various medical conditions."}{"title": "FARMACOL\u00d3GICO:Pharmacological factors can stimulate the secretion of ADH, leading to SIADH, as discussed in the text."}{"title": "HIPOANTREMIA:HIPOANTREMIA refers to a common water metabolism disorder known as hiponatremia, which is particularly prevalent among hospitalized patients, especially those who are receiving artificial nutrition."}{"title": "SOLUCI\u00d3N SALINA HIPERT\u00d3NICA:Soluci\u00f3n Salina Hipert\u00f3nica is a medical treatment used to correct severe hyponatremia by providing a high concentration of sodium to help reduce cerebral edema."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE DESMIELINIZACI\u00d3N OSM\u00d3TICA:S\u00edndrome de Desmielinizaci\u00f3n Osm\u00f3tica is a serious neurological condition that can occur as a complication of rapid correction of chronic hyponatremia."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO ADECUADO:Adequate treatment refers to the specific medical interventions tailored to correct hyponatremia based on its type and etiology."}{"title": "REVIEWS IN CLINICAL GERONTOLOGY:Reviews in Clinical Gerontology is a publication that features studies and reviews related to clinical gerontology, including topics like hyponatremia."}{"title": "SUERO GLUCOSADO:SUERO GLUCOSADO, or glucose solution, is a type of intravenous fluid utilized in medical treatments. It plays a crucial role in managing sodium levels in patients and is particularly important in the treatment of hyponatremia. This solution is often used in conjunction with treatments for patients receiving artificial nutrition, aiding in the management of fluid balance."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT DE ATENCI\u00d3N:Deficit de atenci\u00f3n refers to attention deficits, which can occur in patients with hyponatremia and is categorized under mild neurological symptoms."}{"title": "ALT. MEMORIA:Alteraciones de memoria refers to memory disturbances, which can be symptoms of hyponatremia and are categorized under mild neurological symptoms."}{"title": "MARCHA INESTABLE:Marcha inestable refers to unstable gait, which can be a symptom of hyponatremia and is categorized under mild neurological symptoms."}{"title": "ALT. COGNITIVA:Alteraciones cognitivas refer to cognitive disturbances, which can occur in patients with hyponatremia and are categorized under mild neurological symptoms."}{"title": "DESORIENTACI\u00d3N:Desorientaci\u00f3n refers to disorientation, which can be a symptom of hyponatremia and is categorized under moderate neurological symptoms."}{"title": "SOMNOLENCIA:Somnolencia refers to drowsiness, which can be a symptom of hyponatremia and is categorized under moderate neurological symptoms."}{"title": "CONFUSI\u00d3N:Confusi\u00f3n refers to confusion, which can be a symptom of hyponatremia and is categorized under moderate neurological symptoms."}{"title": "ESTUPOR:Estupor refers to stupor, which can be a severe symptom of hyponatremia."}{"title": "DISTRES RESPIRATORIO:Distress respiratorio refers to respiratory distress, which can be a severe symptom of hyponatremia."}{"title": "HIPONATREMIA HIPOVOL\u00c9MICA:Hiponatremia hipovol\u00e9mica refers to a type of hyponatremia caused by low blood volume."}{"title": "HIPONATREMIA EUVOL\u00c9MICA:Hiponatremia euvol\u00e9mica es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que se presenta en pacientes que reciben nutrici\u00f3n artificial. Se caracteriza por niveles bajos de sodio en la sangre, pero sin una disminuci\u00f3n del volumen de l\u00edquido corporal. En este tipo de hiponatremia, el volumen sangu\u00edneo se mantiene normal, lo que distingue a esta condici\u00f3n de otras formas de hiponatremia que pueden estar asociadas con una reducci\u00f3n del volumen de l\u00edquido."}{"title": "HIPONATREMIA HIPERVOL\u00c9MICA:Hiponatremia hipervol\u00e9mica refers to a type of hyponatremia caused by high blood volume."}{"title": "CIRROSIS CON ASCITIS:Cirrhosis con ascitis refers to cirrhosis with ascites, which can lead to hypervolemic hyponatremia."}{"title": "CONIVAPT\u00c1N:Conivapt\u00e1n is a medication that functions as a vasopressin receptor antagonist, specifically designed to treat hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood. It is administered intravenously and works by antagonizing the effects of antidiuretic hormone (ADH), thereby helping to restore normal sodium levels in patients."}{"title": "FURST:La f\u00f3rmula de Furst es un c\u00e1lculo utilizado para estimar la capacidad renal de eliminar agua libre, relevante en el manejo de la hiponatremia."}{"title": "INTOXICACI\u00d3N AGUDA DE AGUA:La intoxicaci\u00f3n aguda de agua es una condici\u00f3n que puede llevar a hiponatremia, resultando de la ingesta excesiva de agua en un corto per\u00edodo de tiempo."}{"title": "FURSEMIDE:Furosemide is a medication used to promote the elimination of free water in patients with SIADH, administered either intravenously or orally."}{"title": "AZOTEMIA:Azotemia is a medical condition characterized by an excess of nitrogenous waste products in the blood, often due to kidney dysfunction."}{"title": "FURST FORMULA:The Furst formula is a calculation utilized in the medical field to estimate renal capacity for eliminating free water, particularly in patients diagnosed with Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). Additionally, it serves as a method for calculating sodium and potassium levels in patients experiencing hyponatremia. This dual application highlights the formula's importance in managing electrolyte imbalances and assessing renal function in specific clinical scenarios."}{"title": "ALGORITMO MULTIDISCIPLINAR:The \"ALGORITMO MULTIDISCIPLINAR\" is a comprehensive multidisciplinary algorithm designed for the management of hyponatremia, particularly in cases secondary to the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). This algorithm offers detailed guidelines for treatment options, ensuring effective management of hyponatremia in patients. It is especially relevant for individuals receiving artificial nutrition, providing tailored recommendations to address their specific needs. Overall, the algorithm serves as a crucial tool for healthcare professionals in optimizing the care of patients with hyponatremia."}{"title": "HEMORRAGIA SUBARACNOIDEA:Hemorragia subaracnoidea (Subarachnoid Hemorrhage) is a condition that can lead to SIADH and has a specific treatment duration."}{"title": "MASAS CEREBRALES:Masas cerebrales (Brain Tumors) can cause SIADH and affect treatment duration based on the underlying disease evolution."}{"title": "LESIONES CEREBRALES INFLAMATORIAS:Lesiones cerebrales inflamatorias (Inflammatory Brain Injuries) can induce SIADH and affect treatment response."}{"title": "IDIOP\u00c1TICO:Idiop\u00e1tico (Idiopathic) refers to cases of SIADH with no known cause, affecting treatment duration."}{"title": "ELEVADAS TRANSAMINASAS:Elevated transaminases refer to a potential side effect of medications, which is monitored during treatment for SIADH."}{"title": "AGUAS:"}{"title": "FURSEMIDA:FURSEMIDA, also known as Furosemide, is a diuretic medication primarily utilized to treat fluid retention. It is particularly effective in managing conditions associated with excess fluid accumulation in the body. Additionally, Furosemide is employed in the treatment of patients experiencing hyponatremia, especially those who are receiving artificial nutrition. This medication plays a crucial role in regulating fluid balance and electrolyte levels in various clinical settings."}{"title": "HIPOANTREMIA GRAVE:Severe hyponatremia is a critical condition that requires immediate medical intervention, often involving hypertonic saline."}{"title": "HIPO-NATREMIA:Hipo-natremia refers to a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, which can be caused by various factors including fluid imbalance and hormonal issues."}{"title": "HIPO-NATREMIA HIPOVOL\u00c9MICA:Hypo-natremia hypovolemic is a specific type of hyponatremia caused by a decrease in blood volume, often due to fluid loss."}{"title": "HIPO-NATREMIA HIPERVOLEMICA:Hypo-natremia hypervolemic is a type of hyponatremia that occurs when there is an excess of fluid in the body, diluting sodium levels."}{"title": "SFS:SFS (Saline Solution) is a solution used for rehydration and electrolyte balance"}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N AVANZADA:Advanced Nutrition refers to specialized nutritional support strategies used in complex medical conditions"}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA AGUDA:Acute heart failure is a sudden inability of the heart to pump effectively, which can lead to fluid overload and hyponatremia"}{"title": "HYPOANTREMIA:Hyponatremia is a medical condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, which can lead to various health complications."}{"title": "SALT-1 TRIAL:The SALT-1 trial is a clinical study that evaluated the efficacy of tolvaptan in patients with the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion."}{"title": "SALT-2 TRIAL:The SALT-2 trial is a clinical study that further assessed the use of tolvaptan in treating hyponatremia."}{"title": "CLINICAL ENDOCRINOLOGY:Clinical Endocrinology is a journal dedicated to publishing research and reviews on various aspects of clinical endocrinology. It focuses on a range of topics, including adrenal insufficiency and hyponatremia, providing a platform for studies that contribute to the understanding and management of these conditions. The journal serves as a valuable resource for professionals in the field, facilitating the dissemination of important findings and advancements in endocrinology."}{"title": "NEPHRON PHYSIOLOGY:Nephron Physiology is a journal that focuses on research related to kidney function and disorders, including hyponatremia."}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF KIDNEY DISEASES:The International Journal of Kidney Diseases publishes research related to kidney health, including studies on hyponatremia and its effects."}{"title": "MOUNT DB:Mount DB is an author of a study on mortality after hospitalization with hyponatremia."}{"title": "CURHAN GC:Curhan GC is an author of a study on mortality after hospitalization with hyponatremia."}{"title": "HOORN EJ:Hoorn EJ is a researcher and author who has focused on the effects of mild hyponatremia on health outcomes. Through their studies, Hoorn EJ has contributed to the understanding of hyponatremia and its clinical implications, highlighting its significance in medical research and patient care."}{"title": "ZIETSE R:Zietse R is an author who has contributed to research on hyponatremia and its effects on mortality."}{"title": "ANDERSON RJ:Anderson RJ is an author who has conducted a prospective analysis of hyponatremia's epidemiology."}{"title": "CHUNG HM:Chung HM is an author involved in research on hyponatremia and its clinical outcomes."}{"title": "KLUGE R:Kluge R is an author who has studied the epidemiology of hyponatremia."}{"title": "SCHRIER RW:Schrier RW is a co-author who has contributed to research on oral tolvaptan, a medication used in the treatment of certain conditions related to fluid balance. Additionally, Schrier RW has conducted research on the pathogenetic role of vasopressin in hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood. Through these contributions, Schrier RW has played a significant role in advancing the understanding of vasopressin's impact on fluid regulation and its implications for hyponatremia."}{"title": "GILL GV:Gill GV is an author who has studied the characteristics and outcomes of severe hyponatremia."}{"title": "HUDA MSB:Huda MSB is an author who has contributed to research on severe hyponatremia."}{"title": "WILE D:Wile D is an author involved in the study of severe hyponatremia."}{"title": "BOYD A:Boyd A is an author who has researched the outcomes of severe hyponatremia."}{"title": "SKAGEN K:Skagen K is an author who has studied the characteristics of severe hyponatremia."}{"title": "WATSON ID:Watson ID is an author who has contributed to research on severe hyponatremia."}{"title": "CHAWLA A:Chawla A is an author who has studied the mortality associated with hyponatremia."}{"title": "STEARNS RH:Stearns RH is an author who has researched hyponatremia as a risk factor for inpatient mortality."}{"title": "NIGWEKAR SU:Nigwekar SU is an author recognized for contributions to the study of hyponatremia treatment and its impact on patient outcomes. Through their research, Nigwekar SU has explored the complexities of hyponatremia, focusing on both therapeutic approaches and the effects of this condition on the health and recovery of patients."}{"title": "CAPPUCCIO JD:Cappuccio JD is an author who has researched the relationship between mortality and serum sodium levels."}{"title": "WALD R:Wald R is an author who has studied the impact of hospital-associated hyponatremia on patient outcomes."}{"title": "JABER BL:Jaber BL is an author who has researched the effects of hyponatremia on selected outcomes."}{"title": "PRICE LL:Price LL is an author who has studied the impact of hyponatremia on patient outcomes."}{"title": "CORONA G:Corona G is an author who has conducted a meta-analysis on moderate hyponatremia and mortality risk."}{"title": "GIULIANI C:Giuliani C is an author who has contributed to research on hyponatremia and mortality."}{"title": "PARENTI G:Parenti G is an author involved in the study of hyponatremia and its effects."}{"title": "NORELLO D:Norello D is an author who has researched the relationship between hyponatremia and mortality."}{"title": "FORTI G:Forti G is an author who has contributed to research on hyponatremia and its clinical implications."}{"title": "DASTA JF:Dasta JF is an author who has evaluated costs associated with hyponatremia treatment."}{"title": "CHIONG JR:Chiong JR is an author involved in research on hyponatremia and its treatment outcomes."}{"title": "CHIODO III JA:Chiodo III JA is an author who has studied the treatment practices for hyponatremia."}{"title": "GREENBERG A:Greenberg A is an author recognized for their contributions to the field of medicine, particularly in the area of hyponatremia. They have been involved in the expert panel recommendations on hyponatremia, which were published in the American Journal of Medicine. Additionally, Greenberg A has reported on current treatment practices for this condition, further demonstrating their expertise and commitment to advancing knowledge in this important medical area."}{"title": "HYUNSOO OH:HyunSoo Oh is an author who has studied the effects of nasogastric tube feeding on serum sodium levels."}{"title": "YEONOK SUH:YeonOK Suh is an author who has researched the effects of nasogastric tube feeding on serum sodium levels."}{"title": "SUNKYUNG HWANG:SunKyung Hwang is an author who has studied the effects of nasogastric tube feeding on serum sodium levels."}{"title": "WHASOOK SEO:WhaSook Seo is an author who has researched the effects of nasogastric tube feeding on serum sodium levels."}{"title": "TZOULIS P:Tzoulis P is an author who has conducted a case-control study on hyponatremia as a risk factor for inpatient mortality."}{"title": "BAGKERIS E:Bagkeris E is an author who has studied the impact of hyponatremia on inpatient mortality."}{"title": "BOULOUX P-M:Bouloux P-M is an author who has researched the effects of hyponatremia on patient outcomes.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "SALT-1:SALT-1 is a clinical trial related to the study of inappro