"}{"title": "HAAS CS:Haas CS is an author who discussed renal tubular acidosis type IV in hyperkalemic patients, published in Clin Endocrinol Oxf."}{"title": "HANNON MJ:Hannon MJ is an author who studied hyponatremia following subarachnoid hemorrhage, published in J Clin Endocrinol Metab."}{"title": "JANICIC N:Janicic N is an author who discussed the evaluation and management of hypo-osmolality in hospitalized patients, published in Endocrinol Metab Clin North Am."}{"title": "INTERN MED J:Intern Med J is a medical journal that publishes research articles on internal medicine, including studies on hyponatremia."}{"title": "BRITISH JOURNAL OF BIOMEDICAL SCIENCE:Br J Biomed Sci is a journal that publishes research on biomedical science, including studies on electrolyte measurements."}{"title": "J CRIT CARE:J Crit Care is a journal that publishes research on critical care medicine, including studies on sodium measurements in critically ill patients."}{"title": "EUROPEAN CONGRESS OF ENDOCRINOLOGY:The 17th Eur Congr Endocrinol is a conference where research related to endocrinology, including studies on hyponatremia, is presented."}{"title": "AMERICAN J MED:"}{"title": "HILLER A:"}{"title": "ENDOCRINOL METAB CLIN NORTH AM:Journal that published an evaluation and management study on hypo-osmolality in hospitalized patients in 2003"}{"title": "ENDOCR ABSTR TH EUR CONGR ENDOCRINOL:Journal that published abstracts from the European Congress of Endocrinology in 2013"}{"title": "SEMIN NEFROL:Journal that published a study on the treatment of hyponatremia in 2009"}{"title": "CURR OPIN CRIT CARE:Journal that published a review on the diagnosis and management of hyponatremia in acute illness in 2008"}{"title": "NEFROL MADR:Journal that published a multidisciplinary algorithm for treating hyponatremia secondary to SIADH in 2014"}{"title": "NEUROLOGY:Journal that published a study on the reversal of transtentorial herniation with hypertonic saline in 2008"}{"title": "J CARD FAIL:Journal that published a clinical course study of patients with hyponatremia and heart failure in 2013"}{"title": "57.\u00ba CONGR SOC ESP ENDOCRINO:The 57th Congress of the Spanish Society of Endocrinology held in Dublin, Ireland in 2015"}{"title": "ENDOCRINOL NUTR:ENDOCRINOL NUTR is a journal that has contributed to the field of endocrinology and nutrition by publishing significant studies and reviews. In 2013, it published a study focused on the management of hyponatremia caused by the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), conducted by the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service of Hospital Cl\u00ednico San Carlos. Additionally, in 2014, the journal published a systematic review examining the use of urea as a treatment option for managing SIADH. These publications highlight the journal's commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "CRIT CARE:CRIT CARE is a journal dedicated to publishing research in the field of critical care medicine, encompassing a wide range of topics, including pediatric care. In 2010, the journal featured a study focused on the treatment of euvolemic hyponatremia within the intensive care unit, highlighting its commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in critical care settings."}{"title": "NEPHRON CLIN PR:Journal that published a long-term treatment study of hyponatremic patients with nephrogenic syndrome in 2012"}{"title": "PROC SOC EXP BIOL MED:Journal that published research on renal clearance of calcium, magnesium, and inorganic phosphate in 1966"}{"title": "CUESTA HERN\u00c1NDEZ M:Cuesta Hern\u00e1ndez M is a co-author who has contributed to research on the management of hyponatremia, specifically in a study involving the medication tolvaptan."}{"title": "F\u00c9RNANDEZ CAPEL F:Fern\u00e1ndez Capel F is an author involved in studies on hyponatremia and parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "RUIZ GRACIA T:Ruiz Gracia T is an author recognized for contributions to the field of medicine, particularly in the diagnosis and management of hyponatremia. Additionally, Ruiz Gracia T has reported on the progressive reduction of tolvaptan doses in the treatment of chronic Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). Through these works, Ruiz Gracia T has provided valuable insights into effective treatment strategies for these conditions."}{"title": "MART\u00cdN MAT\u00cdA P:Mart\u00edn Mat\u00eda P is an author contributing to research on hyponatremia in hospitalized patients."}{"title": "RUBIO HERRERA MA:Rubio Herrera MA is an author involved in studies related to hyponatremia and parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "STEARNS R:Stearns R is an author who published research on the treatment of hyponatremia."}{"title": "HIX JK:Hix JK is an author involved in research on hyponatremia treatment."}{"title": "KOENIG MA:Koenig MA is an author who published a study on transtentorial herniation treatment."}{"title": "BRYAN M:Bryan M is an author who contributed to research on hypertonic saline treatment."}{"title": "LEWIN JL:Lewin JL is an author involved in studies on neurological conditions."}{"title": "MIRSKI MA:Mirski MA is an author who published research on neurological treatments."}{"title": "GEOCADIN RG:Geocadin RG is an author involved in studies related to neurological conditions."}{"title": "STEVENS RD:Stevens RD is an author who contributed to research on neurological treatments."}{"title": "ODONNELL M:O'Donnell M is an author involved in research on urinary sodium and potassium excretion."}{"title": "MENTE A:Mente A is an author who contributed to studies on cardiovascular events."}{"title": "RANGARAJAM S:Rangarajam S is an author involved in research on cardiovascular health."}{"title": "MC QUEEN MJ:Mc Queen MJ is an author who published research on cardiovascular events."}{"title": "LUI L:Lui L is an author who contributed to research on cardiovascular health."}{"title": "LICATA G:Licata G is an author involved in studies on heart failure treatments."}{"title": "DI PASQUALE:Di Pasquale is an author who contributed to research on heart failure."}{"title": "PARRINELLO G:Parrinello G is an author involved in studies on heart failure treatments."}{"title": "CARDINALE A:Cardinale A is an author who published research on heart failure management."}{"title": "SCANDWA A:Scandwa A is an author involved in studies on heart failure treatments."}{"title": "FOLLONE G:Follone G is an author who contributed to research on heart failure management."}{"title": "HAUPTMAN PJ:Hauptman PJ is an author involved in studies on heart failure and hyponatremia."}{"title": "BURNETT J:Burnett J is an author who published research on heart failure treatments."}{"title": "GHEORGHIADE M:Gheorghiade M is an author involved in studies on heart failure management."}{"title": "GRINFELD L:Grinfeld L is an author who contributed to research on heart failure treatments."}{"title": "KONSTAM MA:Konstam MA is an author involved in studies on heart failure management."}{"title": "KOSTIC D:Kostic D is an author who published research on heart failure treatments."}{"title": "GUPTA S:Gupta S is an author who contributed to research on SIADH."}{"title": "YUNUS S:Yunus S is an author involved in studies on SIADH."}{"title": "TORMEY W:Tormey W is an author who published research on SIADH."}{"title": "THOMPSON C:Thompson C is an author involved in studies on SIADH."}{"title": "DE SOL\u00c1-MORALES O:De Sol\u00e1-Morales O is an author known for conducting a systematic review on the use of urea for managing inappropriate secretion of antidiuretic hormone (ADH), specifically in the context of the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH)."}{"title": "RIERA M:Riera M is a co-author of a systematic review focused on the use of urea for managing inappropriate secretion of antidiuretic hormone (ADH). Additionally, Riera M has contributed to various studies concerning the management of Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH)."}{"title": "CHAPMAN LC:Chapman LC is an author who contributed to research on renal clearance of calcium, magnesium, and inorganic phosphate in humans."}{"title": "VARRADY PD:Varrady PD is an author who collaborated on the study of urea-saline diuresis and its effects on renal clearance."}{"title": "KLEEMAN CR:Kleeman CR is an author involved in the research regarding renal clearance and urea-saline diuresis."}{"title": "DECAUX G:Decaux G is an author who researched the treatment of inappropriate secretion of antidiuretic hormone with furosemide."}{"title": "WATERLOT Y:Waterlot Y is a co-author of the study on inappropriate secretion of antidiuretic hormone treated with furosemide."}{"title": "GENETTE F:Genette F is a co-author involved in the research on inappropriate secretion of antidiuretic hormone."}{"title": "HALLEMANS R:Hallemans R is a co-author of the study on inappropriate secretion of antidiuretic hormone."}{"title": "DEMANET JC:Demanet JC is a co-author who contributed to the research on inappropriate secretion of antidiuretic hormone."}{"title": "ZELTSER D:Zeltser D is a co-author of the study on the efficacy and safety of conivaptan."}{"title": "SMITH N:Smith N is a co-author involved in the assessment of conivaptan for hyponatremic neuro-ICU patients."}{"title": "BARVE A:Barve A is a co-author of the study on conivaptan in patients with euvolemic hyponatremia."}{"title": "ANDOH M:Andoh M is a co-author who contributed to the study on conivaptan."}{"title": "BERL T:Berl T is an author involved in the research on the safety and effectiveness of oral tolvaptan in chronic hyponatremia."}{"title": "QUITTNAT-PELLETIER F:Quittnat-Pelletier F is a co-author of the study on oral tolvaptan."}{"title": "BICHET DG:Bichet DG is a co-author involved in the study on oral tolvaptan."}{"title": "OUYANG J:Ouyang J is a co-author of the research on oral tolvaptan."}{"title": "SALTWATER INVESTIGATORS:The SALTWATER Investigators is a group that conducted research on the safety and effectiveness of oral tolvaptan in chronic hyponatremia."}{"title": "GOMEZ HOYOS E:Gomez Hoyos E is a co-author involved in the study on tolvaptan for treating hyponatremia."}{"title": "RECIO BL\u00c1ZQUEZ L:Recio Bl\u00e1zquez L is a co-author of the research on tolvaptan."}{"title": "DE MIGUEL NOVOA MP:De Miguel Novoa MP is a co-author of the research on tolvaptan."}{"title": "ORTOL\u00c1 A:Ortol\u00e1 A is a co-author involved in the study on tolvaptan doses in chronic SIADH."}{"title": "CRESPO I:Crespo I is a co-author of the research on tolvaptan in chronic SIADH treatment."}{"title": "SANTIAGO A:Santiago A is a co-author involved in the study on tolvaptan."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PEDI\u00c1TRICA:NUTRICI\u00d3N PEDI\u00c1TRICA is a specialized field of medicine dedicated to addressing the nutritional needs and dietary management of infants and children. This area encompasses a comprehensive range of topics, including dietary recommendations for various age groups, focusing on essential macronutrients and micronutrients necessary for healthy growth and development. \n\nThe guidelines within NUTRICI\u00d3N PEDI\u00c1TRICA emphasize the importance of appropriate sodium intake, milk consumption, and the gradual introduction of diverse foods to stimulate appetite and meet nutritional requirements. It also addresses the energy needs and nutrient intake during different stages of childhood, ensuring that dietary plans are tailored to support both undernutrition and overnutrition.\n\nFurthermore, NUTRICI\u00d3N PEDI\u00c1TRICA includes nutritional assessments and interventions aimed at promoting optimal growth and health in pediatric patients. It provides specific dietary guidelines for critical conditions, focusing on medical nutrition therapy and the administration of parenteral nutrition for those with particular medical needs. The field also highlights the significance of enteral nutrition as the preferred method for delivering nutrients to children, ensuring that their dietary needs are met effectively.\n\nOverall, NUTRICI\u00d3N PEDI\u00c1TRICA is essential for guiding healthcare professionals in the nutritional support and dietary management of infants, children, and adolescents, ultimately promoting their health and development."}{"title": "CONIVAPTAN:Conivaptan is a medication used for the treatment of hyponatremia, particularly in patients with euvolemic hyponatremia."}{"title": "TOLVAPTAN:"}{"title": "CL\u00cdNICO UNIVERSITARIO VALENCIA:Cl\u00ednico Universitario Valencia is an institution focused on clinical nutrition and diet therapy, providing educational resources and research in the field of pediatric nutrition."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS NUTRICIONALES:Trastornos Nutricionales refers to nutritional disorders that can affect children, which are addressed through clinical evaluation and intervention."}{"title": "DESNUTRICI\u00d3N AGUDA:Desnutrici\u00f3n Aguda is a condition characterized by a rapid loss of weight and body mass due to inadequate nutrition, particularly relevant in pediatric care."}{"title": "DESNUTRICI\u00d3N CR\u00d3NICA:Desnutrici\u00f3n Cr\u00f3nica refers to long-term undernutrition that affects growth and development in children."}{"title": "PEDIATRIC PATIENT:Pediatric patients are children who are assessed for their nutritional status and health, with a particular focus on their growth and dietary intake."}{"title": "TANNER STAGES:The Tanner Stages are a classification system used to assess the stages of pubertal development in children."}{"title": "UNDERNUTRITION:Undernutrition is a condition resulting from insufficient nutrient intake, leading to health problems such as stunted growth in children."}{"title": "CLINICAL EXAMINATION:Clinical examination is a systematic approach to assess a patient's health, particularly focusing on physical signs of nutritional status in children."}{"title": "HEALTH RECORD:Health records are documents that contain information about a patient's medical history, including dietary habits and growth patterns."}{"title": "CHILD:Children are individuals in the developmental stage of life, typically under the age of 18, who are assessed for health and nutritional status."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL DISORDER:"}{"title": "ADULTS:Adults are individuals who have reached maturity and have stable body mass compared to children."}{"title": "HEIGHT:Height is a fundamental anthropometric measure that evaluates the length or stature of an individual, important for growth assessment."}{"title": "HEAD CIRCUMFERENCE:Head circumference is a measurement used to assess brain development and growth in infants and young children."}{"title": "ARM CIRCUMFERENCE:Arm circumference is a measurement that helps evaluate body composition and nutritional status, particularly in children."}{"title": "TRICEP SKINFOLD:Tricep skinfold measurement assesses subcutaneous fat and helps evaluate body fat percentage and nutritional status."}{"title": "SUBSCAPULAR SKINFOLD:Subscapular skinfold measurement is used to assess body fat distribution and overall nutritional status."}{"title": "WEIGHT:"}{"title": "ORBEGOZO:Orbegozo is an organization that published growth reference patterns for children in Spain, with editions dating back to 1988."}{"title": "CARRASCOSA ET AL.:Carrascosa et al. is a research group that conducted a study highlighting the obesity trend among Spanish children."}{"title": "EURO-GROWTH 2000:Euro-Growth 2000 is a multicentric study that established growth patterns for European children aged 0-5 years."}{"title": "NCHS:The National Center for Health Statistics (NCHS) is an organization that provides data on the growth and nutrition of school-aged children and adolescents in the United States. However, it is important to note that the NCHS was replaced by the CDC's 2000 growth standards in the United States, indicating a shift in the authority and standards used for assessing growth and nutrition in this demographic."}{"title": "BRAZIL:Brazil is one of the countries included in the WHO's international growth reference patterns for children."}{"title": "INDIA:India is a country that plays a significant role in providing data on child growth and nutrition within the context of the World Health Organization (WHO). It is also included in the WHO's international growth reference patterns for children, contributing to global standards and understanding of child health and development."}{"title": "GHANA:Ghana is a country that plays a significant role in providing data on child growth and nutrition within the context of the World Health Organization (WHO). It is included in the WHO's international growth reference patterns for children, which contributes to the global understanding of child growth. Through its participation, Ghana aids in the development of comprehensive insights into the nutritional status and growth patterns of children, thereby supporting global health initiatives."}{"title": "OMAN:Oman is included in the WHO's international growth reference patterns for children, reflecting diverse socioeconomic conditions."}{"title": "NORUEGA:Noruega es un pa\u00eds que proporciona datos sobre el crecimiento infantil y nutrici\u00f3n en el contexto de la OMS."}{"title": "OM\u00c1N:Om\u00e1n es un pa\u00eds que proporciona datos sobre el crecimiento infantil y nutrici\u00f3n en el contexto de la OMS."}{"title": "PATRONES PERCENTILADOS:Los patrones percentilados son herramientas utilizadas para evaluar el crecimiento y el estado nutricional de los ni\u00f1os en comparaci\u00f3n con est\u00e1ndares de referencia."}{"title": "GURNEY AND JELLIFFE:Gurney and Jelliffe are referenced for their nomogram used to calculate muscle area in nutritional assessments."}{"title": "HEMATOL\u00d3GIA:Hematology is a field of study that focuses on blood disorders, including anemia associated with malnutrition."}{"title": "ALBUMINA S\u00c9RICA:Serum albumin is a protein that reflects the nutritional status and synthesis capacity of the liver."}{"title": "ANEMIA CARENCIAL:Deficiency anemia is a condition that occurs when the body does not have enough healthy red blood cells due to a lack of iron, which is often associated with malnutrition."}{"title": "DESNUTRICI\u00d3N AGUDA MODERADA:Moderate acute malnutrition is a condition characterized by a significant weight loss or low weight-for-height in children, indicating a serious health risk."}{"title": "DESNUTRICI\u00d3N AGUDA GRAVE:Severe acute malnutrition is a life-threatening condition that occurs when a child is extremely thin for their height or has nutritional edema."}{"title": "DESNUTRICI\u00d3N CR\u00d3NICA MODERADA:Moderate chronic malnutrition is characterized by low height-for-age, indicating long-term nutritional deficiencies."}{"title": "DESNUTRICI\u00d3N CR\u00d3NICA GRAVE:Severe chronic malnutrition is a serious condition where a child is significantly shorter than the average for their age due to prolonged nutritional deficiencies."}{"title": "\u00cdNDICES ERITROCITARIOS:Erythrocyte indices are measurements used to evaluate the size and hemoglobin content of red blood cells, which can indicate nutritional status."}{"title": "RECUENTO DE RETICULOCITOS:Reticulocyte count is a test that measures the number of young red blood cells in the blood, which can help assess bone marrow function and response to anemia."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ COSTA C.:Mart\u00ednez Costa C. is an author who contributed to the bibliography on the assessment of nutritional status in children."}{"title": "ARGUELLES MART\u00cdN F.:Arguelles Mart\u00edn F. is an author who contributed to the bibliography on the assessment of nutritional status in children."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA NOVO MD:Garc\u00eda Novo MD is a notable author and editor in the field of pediatric nutrition. He has contributed significantly to the bibliography on the assessment of nutritional status in children, enhancing the understanding and evaluation of children's dietary needs. Additionally, Garc\u00eda Novo MD plays a crucial role as an editor in the publication of pediatric nutrition guidelines, further establishing his expertise and influence in this important area of healthcare."}{"title": "PAV\u00d3N:Pav\u00f3n is an author who contributed to the bibliography on the assessment of nutritional status in children."}{"title": "IMPIDANCIA BIOEL\u00c9CTRICA (BIA):Bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA) is a technique used to assess body composition, particularly in children."}{"title": "DENSITOMETR\u00cdA (DXA):Densitometry (DXA) is an examination that quantifies bone mineral content, important for children with dietary deficiencies."}{"title": "RADIOGRAF\u00cdA DE CARPO:Wrist radiography is an essential examination for assessing skeletal maturation in children with growth delays."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic malnutrition is a condition often associated with systemic diseases, leading to delays in skeletal maturation."}{"title": "C-REACTIVA PROTE\u00cdNA:"}{"title": "BILBAO:Bilbao is a city in Spain where a growth study was conducted."}{"title": "GROWTH STANDARDS:Growth standards refer to the benchmarks established for assessing the growth and development of children."}{"title": "PAV\u00d3N RELINCH\u00d3N P:Pav\u00f3n Relinch\u00f3n P is an editor who contributed to the Tratado de Gastroenterolog\u00eda, Hepatolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n Pedi\u00e1trica."}{"title": "ROM\u00c1N RIECHMAN E:Rom\u00e1n Riechman E is an editor associated with the Tratado de Gastroenterolog\u00eda, Hepatolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n Pedi\u00e1trica."}{"title": "SILVA GARC\u00cdA G:Silva Garc\u00eda G is an editor who contributed to the Tratado de Gastroenterolog\u00eda, Hepatolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n Pedi\u00e1trica."}{"title": "SOJO AGUIRRE A:Sojo Aguirre A is an editor involved in the publication of pediatric nutrition guidelines."}{"title": "ERGO:ERGO is a publishing house known for its contributions to the field of pediatric nutrition. It has published several works on this subject, including a comprehensive manual specifically focused on pediatric nutrition."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N FAUSTINO ORBEGOZO:Fundaci\u00f3n Faustino Orbegozo is an organization that conducted a growth study in Bilbao."}{"title": "AN PEDIATR (BARC):An Pediatr (Barc) is a journal that publishes articles related to pediatric health and nutrition."}{"title": "ARGUELLES MART\u00cdN F:"}{"title": "SUSANA REDECILLAS FERREIRO:Susana Redecillas Ferreiro is a medical professional involved in pediatric nutrition and diet therapy."}{"title": "RAQUEL N\u00da\u00d1EZ RAMOS:Raquel N\u00fa\u00f1ez Ramos is a medical professional specializing in pediatric nutrition."}{"title": "RAQUEL LORITE CUENCA:Raquel Lorite Cuenca is a medical professional working in the field of pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition."}{"title": "UNU:The United Nations University (UNU) is an international community of scholars dedicated to addressing global issues through research, capacity development, and the dissemination of knowledge. As an academic and research institution, UNU focuses on conducting research and providing education that contributes to the understanding and resolution of pressing global challenges."}{"title": "ACADEMIA DE CIENCIAS AMERICANA:The American Academy of Sciences is a prestigious organization that promotes scientific research and education in the United States."}{"title": "LACANTES:Infants, specifically those aged 0-1 year, who have specific nutritional requirements for healthy growth and development."}{"title": "TEMA 53:TEMA 53 focuses on dietary recommendations specifically tailored for pediatric patients, emphasizing their unique nutritional needs and the importance of metabolic calculations. This entity provides guidance aimed at ensuring that the dietary requirements of children are adequately met, taking into account their growth and developmental stages."}{"title": "SCHOFIELD:The term \"Schofield\" refers to a set of equations utilized for estimating basal metabolic expenditure, particularly in children, by taking into account their weight and height. These equations are significant in the context of predicting energy requirements for patients, especially pediatric populations. The Schofield equations provide a valuable tool for healthcare professionals in assessing the metabolic needs of children, ensuring appropriate nutritional support and energy balance."}{"title": "NI\u00d1AS:Ni\u00f1as refers to girls, specifically in the context of dietary recommendations and nutritional needs. The energy requirements for this demographic are being calculated in the associated table, highlighting the importance of understanding their nutritional needs."}{"title": "FACTOR DE MULTIPLICACI\u00d3N:Multiplication factors are used to adjust energy expenditure based on clinical situations in pediatric patients."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA MAYOR:Major surgery is a clinical situation that influences energy expenditure in pediatric patients."}{"title": "SEDACI\u00d3N:Sedation is a clinical situation that can decrease energy expenditure in pediatric patients."}{"title": "GASTO METAB\u00d3LICO BASAL:"}{"title": "CANTIDAD:Cantidad refers to the amount of nutrients required in the diet, which is critical for meeting the nutritional needs of children."}{"title": "ACTIVIDAD F\u00cdSICA LIGERA:Light physical activity level as categorized in the energy requirements table."}{"title": "ACTIVIDAD F\u00cdSICA MODERADA:Moderate physical activity level as categorized in the energy requirements table."}{"title": "ACTIVIDAD F\u00cdSICA INTENSA:Intense physical activity level as categorized in the energy requirements table."}{"title": "KCAL/D\u00cdA:Kcal/d\u00eda indicates the daily caloric intake required for girls based on their age and activity level."}{"title": "KCAL/KG/D:Kcal/kg/d represents the caloric intake per kilogram of body weight for girls based on their age and activity level."}{"title": "DIETARY REFERENCE INTAKE:The Dietary Reference Intake (DRI) provides guidelines for nutrient intake levels to meet the needs of most healthy individuals."}{"title": "HOLLIDAY-SEGAR EQUATION:The Holliday-Segar equation is a formula used to calculate fluid requirements for children based on their weight."}{"title": "TABLE 7:Table 7 provides adequate water intake recommendations for children of various ages."}{"title": "TABLE 8:Table 8 details protein requirements for children based on age."}{"title": "TABLE 9:Table 9 discusses the composition of dietary fats and recommendations for fat intake in children."}{"title": "MOTHER'S MILK:Mother's milk is the primary source of nutrition for infants in the first six months, providing essential lipids and fatty acids."}{"title": "LIQUID INTAKE RECOMMENDATIONS:Liquid intake recommendations provide guidelines for the amount of fluid children should consume based on their age."}{"title": "PROTEIN REQUIREMENTS:Protein requirements outline the necessary daily intake of protein for children based on their age and development."}{"title": "NUTRIENT INTAKE:Nutrient intake encompasses the overall consumption of essential vitamins and minerals necessary for a child's growth and health."}{"title": "AAP:AAP is the American Academy of Pediatrics, which offers recommendations and guidelines for pediatric health and nutrition."}{"title": "BOLLER\u00cdA INDUSTRIAL:BOLLER\u00cdA INDUSTRIAL refers to industrially produced baked goods that are often high in sugars and fats, and should be limited in children's diets."}{"title": "AGPI N-6:AGPI n-6 refers to omega-6 fatty acids that are essential for health and should be included in children's diets."}{"title": "AGPI N-3:AGPI n-3 refers to omega-3 fatty acids that are crucial for brain development and overall health in children."}{"title": "NECESIDADES DE MICRONUTRIENTES:NECESIDADES DE MICRONUTRIENTES refers to the essential vitamins and minerals required for children's health."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES DE LA ESPGHAN:RECOMENDACIONES DE LA ESPGHAN are specific dietary guidelines provided by the European Society for Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES DE LA AAP:RECOMENDACIONES DE LA AAP are specific dietary guidelines provided by the American Academy of Pediatrics."}{"title": "LEGISLACI\u00d3N DE LA UNI\u00d3N EUROPEA:LEGISLACI\u00d3N DE LA UNI\u00d3N EUROPEA refers to the laws and regulations set by the European Union that impact nutrition guidelines.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CEREALES RICOS EN FIBRA:Cereales ricos en fibra are high-fiber cereals that contribute to dietary fiber intake."}{"title": "PAN BLANCO:Pan blanco is a type of bread that is low in fiber content."}{"title": "PAN DE MOLDE:Pan de molde is a type of bread that is commonly used for sandwiches and has moderate fiber content."}{"title": "ESPINACAS CONGELADAS:Espinacas congeladas are frozen spinach, a vegetable rich in fiber."}{"title": "GUISANTES CONGELADOS:Guisantes congelados are frozen peas, which are a good source of dietary fiber."}{"title": "LENTEJAS:Lentejas, commonly known as lentils, are legumes that serve as a nutritious food source. They provide 7.1 mg of iron per 100 grams, making them a valuable addition to a diet, particularly for those needing to increase their iron intake. Additionally, lentejas are recognized for being a good source of dietary fiber, contributing to digestive health and overall well-being."}{"title": "ALBARICOQUES:Albaricoques are apricots, a fruit that contains dietary fiber."}{"title": "CEREZAS:Cerezas are cherries, a fruit that provides some dietary fiber."}{"title": "CIRUELAS:Ciruelas are plums that are recognized for their nutritional benefits, providing 3 mg of iron per 100 grams. Additionally, they are known for their high fiber content, making them a healthy choice for those looking to improve their dietary intake."}{"title": "LECHE HUMANA:Human milk is the ideal exclusive food for infants in the first 6 months of life, providing optimal calcium and nutrients"}{"title": "VERDURAS DE HOJA VERDE:Leafy green vegetables are a good source of calcium, particularly those low in oxalates to enhance absorption"}{"title": "6-12 MESES:Age group for infants where specific dietary recommendations for calcium and iron are provided"}{"title": "1-3 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"1-3 A\u00d1OS\" refers to the age group of toddlers, specifically those aged between one to three years. This age group is associated with specific dietary recommendations, particularly concerning the recommended dietary allowances for essential nutrients such as calcium and iron. These guidelines are crucial for supporting the growth and development of children in this formative stage."}{"title": "4-8 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"4-8 a\u00f1os\" refers to the age group of young children, specifically those aged 4 to 8 years old. This age group is significant for various health and demographic statistics, as it encompasses important developmental milestones. There are specific dietary recommendations associated with this age range, particularly concerning calcium intake, which is crucial for healthy growth and development. Additionally, this group is categorized for health metrics and developmental indicators, highlighting the importance of monitoring their well-being during these formative years."}{"title": "9-18 A\u00d1OS:Age group for adolescents with increased dietary needs for calcium and iron"}{"title": "ANEMIA FISIOL\u00d3GICA:Physiological anemia in infants that occurs due to changes in hemoglobin synthesis at birth"}{"title": "0-6 MESES:The term \"0-6 meses\" refers to the age group of infants from birth to 6 months. This period is characterized by specific dietary recommendations tailored to the nutritional needs of infants during their early development."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN CALCIO:Foods rich in calcium are recommended for maintaining adequate calcium levels in the body, especially in children and adolescents."}{"title": "ADOLESCENTES:Adolescents experience increased nutritional demands, particularly for iron and calcium, due to growth spurts."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN HIERRO:Iron-rich foods are recommended for adolescents to prevent iron deficiency and support growth."}{"title": "ALMEJAS:Almejas are a type of shellfish that are rich in iron, providing 24 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "PESCADILLA:Pescadilla is a type of fish that contains 11-13 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "OSTRAS:Ostras are shellfish that provide 6.5 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "MEJILLONES:Mejillones are a type of shellfish that contain 4.2 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "CALAMARES:Calamares are a type of seafood that contains 1.7 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "PULPO:Pulpo is a type of seafood that contains 1.7 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "ACELGAS:Acelgas are leafy greens that contain 3.1 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "VACUNO:Vacuno refers to beef that contains 2.5 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "CERDO:Cerdo refers to pork that contains 1.5 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "PIPAS:Pipas are seeds that contain 6.3 mg of iron per 100 g."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "FL\u00daOR:Fluorine is recommended to prevent dental caries and is primarily sourced from drinking water."}{"title": "PIR\u00c1MIDES DE LA ALIMENTACI\u00d3N:Food pyramids are used as educational models to establish general dietary recommendations."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN MAGNESIO:Foods rich in magnesium include green leafy vegetables, cereals, and nuts, which are important for various bodily functions."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN ZINC:Foods rich in zinc include red meat and seafood, which are essential for growth and immune function."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN SELENIO:Foods rich in selenium include fish, meat, and cereals, which help protect against oxidative stress."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FL\u00daOR:Fluorine is primarily found in drinking water and is important for dental health."}{"title": "TABLAS 17 Y 18:Tablas 17 y 18 provide a guide for the recommended frequencies of food consumption and portion sizes according to age."}{"title": "TABLA 19:Tabla 19 lists the main food sources of essential nutrients."}{"title": "ALMUERZO DE MEDIA MA\u00d1ANA:Almuerzo de media ma\u00f1ana is a mid-morning meal that should provide a portion of the daily nutritional needs."}{"title": "MY PLATE:My Plate is a dietary guideline representation that helps individuals understand food group proportions."}{"title": "PESOS DE RACIONES:Pesos de raciones outlines the recommended weights of food portions and serving sizes for various food groups."}{"title": "PATATAS, ARROZ, PAN, PAN INTEGRAL Y PASTA:This group of foods includes potatoes, rice, bread, whole grain bread, and pasta, which are recommended to be consumed in specific frequencies and portion sizes."}{"title": "3-6 A\u00d1OS:Age group for which specific dietary recommendations are provided"}{"title": "7-12 A\u00d1OS:Age group for which specific dietary recommendations are provided"}{"title": "13-15 A\u00d1OS:Age group for which specific dietary recommendations are provided"}{"title": "16-18 A\u00d1OS:Age group for which specific dietary recommendations are provided"}{"title": "VERDURA COCIDA:Cooked vegetables that are included in the dietary recommendations for children"}{"title": "ZANAHORIAS:Carrots, a vegetable that is part of the recommended daily intake for children"}{"title": "ENSALADA VARIADA:"}{"title": "CEREALES, LEGUMBRES Y TUB\u00c9RCULOS:Cereals, legumes, and tubers are food categories that include rice and pasta, with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes."}{"title": "CARNES Y DERIVADOS, AVES, PESCADOS Y HUEVOS:This category includes various types of meats, poultry, fish, and eggs, with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes."}{"title": "PASTA:Pasta is a type of food categorized under cereals, often served in various dishes, with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes."}{"title": "PAN TIPO BARRA:Pan tipo barra is a type of bread with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes, commonly used in meals."}{"title": "PAN TIPO PAY\u00c9S:Pan tipo pay\u00e9s is a type of rustic bread with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes, often included in meals."}{"title": "FILETE:Filete refers to a cut of meat with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes, commonly used in main dishes."}{"title": "CHULETAS CERDO:Chuletas cerdo are pork chops with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes, typically served as a main dish."}{"title": "COSTILLAS CORDERO:Costillas cordero are lamb ribs with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes, often served in meals."}{"title": "CARNE PICADA:Carne picada refers to ground meat used in various dishes, with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes."}{"title": "FILETE DE PESCADO:Filete de pescado is a type of fish fillet with specific weight measurements for different serving sizes, often served in main dishes."}{"title": "RIVOFLABINA:Riboflavin (Vitamin B2) is essential for energy production and is found in milk, meat, and eggs."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N COMPLEMENTARIA:ALIMENTACI\u00d3N COMPLEMENTARIA refers to the crucial period in an infant's dietary development when complementary foods are introduced alongside breastfeeding. This process typically begins after 17 weeks of age and is recommended to occur before the infant reaches 26 weeks. During this phase, solid foods are gradually incorporated into the infant's diet to ensure they receive adequate nutrition as they grow."}{"title": "BEBIDAS VEGETALES:BEBIDAS VEGETALES are plant-based drinks that are not considered a complete food alternative to cow's milk for infants."}{"title": "ARS\u00c9NICO:ARS\u00c9NICO is a toxic element that can be absorbed by rice plants, posing health risks if consumed in large amounts."}{"title": "PRESI\u00d3N ARTERIAL:PRESI\u00d3N ARTERIAL is a health condition that can be influenced by dietary sodium intake, particularly in genetically predisposed children."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS INFANTILES:F\u00d3RMULAS INFANTILES are infant formulas that may contain hydrolyzed rice protein and should specify their arsenic content."}{"title": "H\u00c1BITOS FAMILIARES:H\u00c1BITOS FAMILIARES refer to family eating habits that can influence children's food preferences and acceptance."}{"title": "SNACKS:SNACKS are intermediate meals that can contribute significantly to a child's total caloric intake."}{"title": "AGENCIA PARA LA INVESTIGACI\u00d3N SOBRE EL C\u00c1NCER:The Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC) is an organization that studies the relationship between diet and cancer risk, particularly focusing on red and processed meat consumption."}{"title": "NI\u00d1O:A child who is the subject of dietary recommendations and nutritional needs."}{"title": "DEPORTE:Sports activities are mentioned in relation to children's increased nutritional requirements and dietary adjustments."}{"title": "DOM\u00cdNGUEZ ORTEGA:F. Dom\u00ednguez Ortega is an author who analyzed the concentration of fatty acids in colostrum and transitional milk."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ SU\u00c1REZ:Mart\u00ednez Su\u00e1rez is an author who provided recommendations on calcium and vitamin D intake for children."}{"title": "WAGNER CL.:Wagner CL. is an author associated with the American Academy of Pediatrics, focusing on the prevention of rickets and vitamin D deficiency."}{"title": "KOLETZKO B.:Koletzko B. is an author who contributed to the global standard for the composition of infant formula."}{"title": "REAL DECRETO 867/2008:REAL DECRETO 867/2008 is a Spanish regulation that establishes technical and sanitary standards for the production of infant formulas and follow-up formulas. It governs the composition and safety of these products, ensuring that they meet specific technical-sanitary regulations in Spain. This regulation plays a crucial role in safeguarding the health and well-being of infants by setting clear guidelines for the formulation and quality of infant nutrition products."}{"title": "GUIDELINE ON FLUORIDE THERAPY:The Guideline on Fluoride Therapy provides recommendations for the use of fluoride in pediatric dentistry."}{"title": "TORUN B.:"}{"title": "ANA BEL\u00c9N MART\u00cdNEZ ZAZO:Ana Bel\u00e9n Mart\u00ednez Zazo is a pediatric specialist and attending physician at Hospital La Moraleja in Madrid, focusing on pediatric nutrition."}{"title": "\u00d3SCAR RUBIO CABEZAS:\u00d3scar Rubio Cabezas is a pediatric specialist and researcher at Hospital Infantil Universitario Ni\u00f1o Jes\u00fas in Madrid, with a focus on pediatric endocrinology."}{"title": "CONSUELO PEDR\u00d3N GINER:Consuelo Pedr\u00f3n Giner is a pediatric specialist and doctor at Hospital Infantil Universitario Ni\u00f1o Jes\u00fas in Madrid, specializing in nutrition and gastroenterology."}{"title": "HOSPITAL LA MORALEJA:Hospital La Moraleja is a medical facility in Madrid specializing in pediatric care."}{"title": "HOSPITAL INFANTIL UNIVERSITARIO NI\u00d1O JES\u00daS:Hospital Infantil Universitario Ni\u00f1o Jes\u00fas is a children's hospital in Madrid that provides specialized pediatric care and research."}{"title": "LANCET ONCOLOGY:Lancet Oncology is a medical journal that publishes research on cancer, including studies on dietary impacts on cancer risk."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS NATURALES:ALIMENTOS NATURALES refers to natural food sources that are utilized in the preparation of nutritional formulas specifically designed for enteral feeding. These foods are also suitable for supplementing the oral diet of pediatric patients, providing essential nutrients in a natural form to support their dietary needs."}{"title": "M\u00d3DULOS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional modules that can be used to enhance the diet of children with inadequate oral intake."}{"title": "PACIENTES PEDI\u00c1TRICOS:"}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE INMUNODEFICIENCIA ADQUIRIDA:A condition that can lead to increased nutritional needs and may require enteral feeding."}{"title": "ATRESIA ESOF\u00c1GICA:Esophageal atresia is a congenital condition where the esophagus does not connect properly, necessitating enteral nutrition."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULA TRAQUEOESOF\u00c1GICA:Tracheoesophageal fistula is a congenital defect that can complicate feeding, often requiring enteral nutrition."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE PIERRE-ROBIN:Pierre-Robin syndrome is a condition that can cause feeding difficulties, often requiring enteral nutrition."}{"title": "NEFROPAT\u00cdA CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic kidney disease can affect nutritional status, often necessitating enteral nutrition."}{"title": "FUNDUPLICATURA DE NISSEN:FUNDUPLICATURA DE NISSEN is a surgical technique used to prevent gastroesophageal reflux, often associated with gastrostomy procedures."}{"title": "PSEUDOBSTRUCCI\u00d3N INTESTINAL CR\u00d3NICA:PSEUDOBSTRUCCI\u00d3N INTESTINAL CR\u00d3NICA is a medical condition characterized by symptoms of intestinal blockage without any physical obstruction."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES EN LA EXCRECI\u00d3N DE NUTRIENTES:ALTERACIONES EN LA EXCRECI\u00d3N DE NUTRIENTES refers to changes in the body's ability to absorb and excrete nutrients, often impacting overall health."}{"title": "FUNDUPLICATURA:La funduplicatura es un procedimiento quir\u00fargico indicado en casos de enfermedad pulmonar asociada al reflujo gastroesof\u00e1gico."}{"title": "BOT\u00d3N DE GASTROSTOM\u00cdA:El bot\u00f3n de gastrostom\u00eda es un dispositivo que permite la colocaci\u00f3n de una v\u00e1lvula unidireccional en el punto de inserci\u00f3n de la gastrostom\u00eda."}{"title": "YEYUNOSTOM\u00cdAS QUIR\u00daRGICAS:Las yeyunostom\u00edas quir\u00fargicas son procedimientos indicados en pacientes con reflujo gastroesof\u00e1gico grave o gastroparesia no controlable."}{"title": "SONDAS TRANSIL\u00d3RICAS:Las sondas transpil\u00f3ricas son dispositivos que se pueden colocar a trav\u00e9s de gastrostom\u00edas preexistentes para la alimentaci\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "BOMBAS DE NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL:Las bombas de nutrici\u00f3n enteral son dispositivos utilizados para administrar f\u00f3rmulas enterales de manera controlada y precisa."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N G\u00c1STRICA INTERMITENTE:La alimentaci\u00f3n g\u00e1strica intermitente es una t\u00e9cnica de administraci\u00f3n de f\u00f3rmulas enterales en forma de bolo, facilitando la transici\u00f3n a la ingesta oral."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL A D\u00c9BITO CONTINUO:La nutrici\u00f3n enteral a d\u00e9bito continuo se administra con una bomba de infusi\u00f3n perist\u00e1ltica, indicada en pacientes con disminuci\u00f3n del \u00e1rea absortiva intestinal."}{"title": "GASTROPEXIA:La gastropexia es una t\u00e9cnica quir\u00fargica utilizada para fijar el est\u00f3mago a la pared abdominal, facilitando la colocaci\u00f3n de una sonda de gastrostom\u00eda."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS COMERCIALES:Commercially prepared nutritional formulas made from various natural food sources, designed for enteral feeding."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS A PARTIR DE ALIMENTOS NATURALES:Nutritional formulas made from natural food sources like meat, eggs, and vegetables, suitable for patients with adequate digestive capacity."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL C\u00cdCLICA:A method of enteral nutrition that combines formula administration during specific hours and intermittent oral feeding."}{"title": "PEDIATRIC FORMULAS:Pediatric formulas are specially designed nutritional products for children aged 1 to 10 years, providing essential vitamins and minerals."}{"title": "DIETIST:A dietist is a professional who specializes in diet and nutrition, playing a crucial role in the assessment and management of malnutrition. They assist in calculating nutritional compositions to ensure that patients achieve adequate nutrient intake, thereby promoting overall health and well-being."}{"title": "CHRONIC NEUROLOGICAL DISEASES:Chronic neurological diseases are conditions that require long-term nutritional support due to compromised digestive functions."}{"title": "MODULAR COMPONENTS:Modular components are nutritional supplements used to modify enteral formulas to meet specific dietary needs."}{"title": "FORMULAS FOR CHILDREN:Formulas for children are specialized nutritional products designed to meet the dietary needs of children over 10 years old."}{"title": "ENSURE JUNIOR DRINK:Ensure Junior Drink is a nutritional formula produced by Abbott, designed for children aged 1-10 years, providing essential nutrients and energy for growth."}{"title": "ENSURE JUNIOR PLUS:Ensure Junior Plus is a nutritional formula produced by Abbott, aimed at children aged 1-10 years, offering additional protein and energy."}{"title": "ENSURE JUNIOR CON FIBRA:Ensure Junior con fibra is a nutritional formula by Abbott, tailored for children aged 1-10 years, enriched with fiber for digestive health."}{"title": "ENSURE JUNIOR PLUS CON FIBRA:Ensure Junior Plus con Fibra is a nutritional formula from Abbott, designed for children aged 1-10 years, combining extra protein and fiber."}{"title": "FREBINI ORIGINAL:Frebini original is a nutritional formula produced by Fresenius-Kabi, suitable for children aged 1-12 years, providing essential nutrients."}{"title": "FORTINI 1.0 MULTI FIBRE:Fortini 1.0 Multi Fibre is a nutritional formula by Nutricia, designed for children aged 1-12 years, offering a balanced mix of nutrients and fiber."}{"title": "FORTINI:Fortini is a nutritional formula produced by Nutricia, suitable for children from 1 year old, providing essential nutrients for growth."}{"title": "FORTINI CF:Fortini CF is a specialized nutritional formula by Nutricia, designed for children over 1 year old, catering to specific dietary needs."}{"title": "FORTINI IBD:Fortini IBD is a nutritional formula developed by Nutricia, specifically aimed at children over the age of 5 who are dealing with inflammatory bowel disease. This product is designed to provide essential nutritional support, featuring specific macronutrient ratios tailored to meet the needs of these children."}{"title": "FORTINI MULTI FIBRE:Fortini Multi Fibre is a nutritional formula produced by Nutricia, designed for children aged 1 year and older. This formula offers a blend of essential nutrients and fiber, making it a suitable option for supporting the dietary needs of young children."}{"title": "FREBINI ENERGY:Frebini Energy is a product by Fresenius-Kabi aimed at children aged 1-12 years, providing energy and essential nutrients."}{"title": "ISOSOURCE JUNIOR:Isosource Junior is a nutritional product by Nestl\u00e9 for children aged 1-10 years, providing balanced nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRINI:Nutrini is a product by Nutricia designed for children aged 1-6 years, offering essential nutrients for growth."}{"title": "FREBINI ENERGY DRINK:Frebini Energy Drink is a product by Fresenius-Kabi aimed at children aged 1-12 years, offering energy and hydration."}{"title": "FREBINI ENERGY FIBRE DRINK:Frebini Energy Fibre Drink is a nutritional product by Fresenius-Kabi for children aged 1-12 years, providing energy and dietary fiber."}{"title": "NUTRINI MF:Nutrini MF is a product by Nutricia designed for children aged 1-6 years, offering a modified formula for specific dietary needs."}{"title": "NUTRINI ENERGY:Nutrini Energy is a nutritional product by Nutricia for children aged 1-6 years, providing additional energy and nutrients."}{"title": "NUTRINI ENERGY MF:Nutrini Energy MF is a product developed by Nutricia specifically designed for children aged 1 to 6 years. It features a modified formula tailored to meet the energy needs of young children, ensuring they receive the appropriate nutrition during this critical stage of growth and development."}{"title": "LACTALIS:Lactalis is a global dairy products company that produces a variety of milk-based nutritional products, including those for infants and children."}{"title": "REAL DECRETO 165/2014:REAL DECRETO 165/2014 is a Spanish regulation that establishes additional standards for the nutritional labeling and composition of infant formulas. It specifically outlines the requirements for infant nutrition products in Spain, ensuring that these products meet certain safety and quality standards for the health and well-being of infants."}{"title": "NUTRINIMAX:Nutrinimax is a nutritional formula by Nutricia for children aged 7-12 years, aimed at providing essential nutrients for growth and development."}{"title": "NUTRINIMAX MF:Nutrinimax MF is a modified version of Nutrinimax, tailored for children aged 7-12 years with specific dietary requirements."}{"title": "NUTRINIMAX ENERGY:Nutrinimax Energy is a high-energy nutritional formula by Nutricia for children aged 7-12 years, focusing on energy needs."}{"title": "NUTRINIMAX ENERGY MF:Nutrinimax Energy MF is a modified high-energy formula for children aged 7-12 years, produced by Nutricia."}{"title": "RESOURCE IBD:Resource IBD is a nutritional product by Nestl\u00e9 designed for children over 5 years with Crohn's disease, providing specialized dietary support."}{"title": "RESOURCE CF:Resource CF is a nutritional formula by Nestl\u00e9 for children aged 1-10 years, formulated to meet the dietary needs of those with cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "RESOURCE JUNIOR:Resource Junior is a nutritional product by Nestl\u00e9 for children aged 1-10 years, providing essential nutrients for growth."}{"title": "RESOURCE JUNIOR FIBRE:Resource Junior Fibre is a fiber-enriched nutritional formula by Nestl\u00e9 for children aged 1-10 years, aimed at promoting digestive health."}{"title": "SANUTRI FQ:Sanutri FQ is a nutritional product by Lactalis for children over 2 years, designed to meet their dietary needs."}{"title": "FORMULAS PARA LACTANTES:Las f\u00f3rmulas para lactantes son sustitutos apropiados para la alimentaci\u00f3n de los lactantes nacidos a t\u00e9rmino durante el primer a\u00f1o de vida."}{"title": "LEGISLACION EUROPEA:La nueva legislaci\u00f3n europea, aplicable en 2020, establece que todas las f\u00f3rmulas para lactantes deben contener DHA en una cantidad espec\u00edfica."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS PARA LACTANTES:"}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS DE SOJA:F\u00d3RMULAS DE SOJA are specialized nutritional preparations made from purified soy protein, designed for infants with specific dietary needs."}{"title": "ALERGIA A PROTE\u00cdNAS DE LECHE DE VACA:ALERGIA A PROTE\u00cdNAS DE LECHE DE VACA is an allergic reaction to proteins found in cow's milk, necessitating alternative formulas for affected infants."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS ESPECIALES ALTERNATIVAS:F\u00d3RMULAS ESPECIALES ALTERNATIVAS are specialized formulas used when standard cow's milk-based formulas are not suitable for infants."}{"title": "L-METIONINA:L-METIONINA is an essential amino acid that plays a crucial role in protein synthesis and metabolism. It is commonly added to soy formulas to ensure adequate protein quality for infants, thereby supporting their growth and development. Additionally, L-METIONINA serves as a precursor for other amino acids, highlighting its importance in various metabolic processes."}{"title": "DIARREA PERSISTENTE:DIARREA PERSISTENTE refers to a condition that may affect infants, requiring special dietary considerations."}{"title": "ENTEROPAT\u00cdA SENSIBLE A LECHE DE VACA:ENTEROPAT\u00cdA SENSIBLE A LECHE DE VACA is a condition in which infants have adverse reactions to cow's milk proteins."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME POSTENTERITIS:S\u00cdNDROME POSTENTERITIS is a condition that can occur in infants after gastrointestinal infections, affecting their dietary needs."}{"title": "APLV:APLV refers to the allergy to cow's milk protein mediated by IgE, which is a condition affecting infants and children."}{"title": "SOY FORMULAS:Soy formulas are dietary products that are contraindicated for premature newborns due to health risks associated with their use."}{"title": "HYDROLYZED FORMULAS:Hydrolyzed formulas are developed for infants with severe allergies to cow's milk proteins and are recommended for children with such allergies or malabsorption issues."}{"title": "ELEMENTAL FORMULAS:Elemental formulas are specialized dietary products designed for children aged 1 to 10 years with specific nutritional needs."}{"title": "PROCTOCOLITIS:Proctocolitis is an inflammatory condition affecting the colon and rectum, which can be associated with allergies in infants."}{"title": "SUCRASE-ISOMALTASE DEFICIENCY:Sucrase-isomaltase deficiency is a condition that affects the digestion of certain sugars, relevant in the context of infant nutrition."}{"title": "COW'S MILK PROTEIN:"}{"title": "ENTEROCOLITIS NECROSANTE:La enterocolitis necrosante es una complicaci\u00f3n grave que puede afectar a los reci\u00e9n nacidos prematuros, caracterizada por la inflamaci\u00f3n y la muerte del tejido intestinal."}{"title": "CPAP:La CPAP (presi\u00f3n positiva continua de la v\u00eda a\u00e9rea) es un m\u00e9todo de soporte respiratorio que se utiliza en reci\u00e9n nacidos prematuros y puede influir en su alimentaci\u00f3n."}¶b0␀␀␀␀␀<c0␀␀␀␀␀Âc0␀␀␀␀␀Jd0␀␀␀␀␀Ωd0␀␀␀␀␀e0␀␀␀␀␀°e0␀␀␀␀␀f0␀␀␀␀␀Uf0␀␀␀␀␀∫f0␀␀␀␀␀Ag0␀␀␀␀␀¨g0␀␀␀␀␀˚g0␀␀␀␀␀`h0␀␀␀␀␀Âh0␀␀␀␀␀Ni0␀␀␀␀␀ôi0␀␀␀␀␀j0␀␀␀␀␀áj0␀␀␀␀␀¯j0␀␀␀␀␀Ik0␀␀␀␀␀¨k0␀␀␀␀␀3l0␀␀␀␀␀Il0␀␀␀␀␀Âl0␀␀␀␀␀ìm0␀␀␀␀␀&n0␀␀␀␀␀ín0␀␀␀␀␀/q0␀␀␀␀␀∆q0␀␀␀␀␀Dr0␀␀␀␀␀ór0␀␀␀␀␀%s0␀␀␀␀␀Ms0␀␀␀␀␀t0␀␀␀␀␀—t0␀␀␀␀␀wu0␀␀␀␀␀v0␀␀␀␀␀»v0␀␀␀␀␀ew0␀␀␀␀␀x0␀␀␀␀␀∫x0␀␀␀␀␀my0␀␀␀␀␀@z0␀␀␀␀␀
